3. She owns a dog who responds to the nickname "dumb dumb" and also to "baby," which was one of her original names. (Verbatim: "i accidentally convinced my dog to respond to the word dumb dumb" and "her official registered name is was baby baby like b-e-b-y baby")

4. She is the only girl among her siblings and has at least two brothers, one older and one younger ("little ellie bro"). (Verbatim: "i have brothers i'm the only girl" and "older ellie bro" and "little ellie bro")

5. She felt she received unfair treatment growing up, being overly protected due to being the only daughter, while her brothers had more freedom. (Verbatim: "we must protect our only girl you must not go outside ever")

6. Her parents used humorously harsh remarks, telling her brothers "no one would want to kidnap their ugly butts but they'd want to kidnap you." (Verbatim: "no one would want to kidnap their ugly butts but they'd want to kidnap you")

7. She attended university and graduated, and her parents jokingly gave her "the brain" they bestowed at birth as a graduation gift. (Verbatim: "the brain that we bestowed upon you when you were birthed that is your gift")

8. She chose a university far from home specifically to gain independence and leave the house. (Verbatim: "as soon as i went to uni i made sure to pick one far so that i could um be out the house")

9. She aspires to showcase her professional gaming skills to her audience in the future. (Verbatim: "maybe what about my professional gaming one day y'all will see my professional gaming skills")

10. She refers to her pre-stream casual chat sessions as "pre-zatsu" and enjoys long, unstructured conversations with her audience. (Verbatim: "i'm not the only one with a long pre-game zatsu" and "gotta have that pre-game chat right") [end of text]



1. She moved out of her family home as soon as she started university for the sake of her mental health. (Verbatim: "as soon as i was able to i was like as soon as i can move out i'm moving out bye... for my mental health")

2. She attended university in England and lived without a washing machine during parts of her student life. (Verbatim: "i didn't have a washing machine in my first year... in my final year the washing machine... you had to pay and put coins in to use it")

3. She frequently returned home during university so her family could do her laundry. (Verbatim: "whenever they'd be like look we'll pay for you to come back and visit and i'd be like okay i'll bring all my clothes and and we can get them all washed yay")

4. She finds coin-operated washing machines unreliable and believes they are designed not to work. (Verbatim: "coin washing machines always ate my coins i'm pretty certain they're designed not to work")

5. She went on a trip to Japan and brought back summer clothing that she needed to wash upon return. (Verbatim: "i have you know i'm on the last washing load for my japan trip... a lot of my the stuff that i wore in japan was like my summer stuff")

6. She splits her wardrobe into seasonal categories: summer and winter. (Verbatim: "i split my wardrobe into summer and winter")

7. She grew up in England and experienced retail work during holidays, which exposed her to repetitive holiday music. (Verbatim: "anyone that's worked in retail has... you'll be listening to christmas songs on repeat until from november")

8. She celebrates British holidays including Halloween, Bonfire Night, Christmas, Easter, New Year, Pancake Day, and Valentine’s Day. (Verbatim: "we have halloween bonfire night christmas... easter new year... pancake day valentine's day")

9. She has a fondness for pancakes and made fluffy pancakes during her trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "i made sure to have fluffy fluffy pancakes in japan... pancakes are just yummy")

10. She played League of Legends in the past and is currently playing Teamfight Tactics, preferring it because she doesn’t have to work in a team. (Verbatim: "i'm actually playing more team fight tactics at the moment... that way i don't have to work in a team") [end of text]



1. She gets nervous when trying new stream ideas and worries about audience reception. (Verbatim: "i get nervous when i do stream ideas... are they gonna hate it it's gonna be boring they're gonna be like damn she sucks up puzzles and then i can judge me and put me in the bin")

